    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW217rvRPAeUUaadDdTZqZRwo)_\n\nFirst of three stacked PRs: **#325 rename + org-detached**, then #326 sidebar, then #327 `vulpea-ui` widget.\n\n## What\n- `sia-vulpea-show-grouped-backlinks` is now `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-org-detached` (the `.org` view, unchanged in behaviour).\n- Helpers take the module prefix:\n  - `sia-vulpea--line-meta-key-at` is now `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks--meta-key-at`\n  - `sia-vulpea-classify-backlinks` is now `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-classify`\n- Old names are removed, with no aliases (ADR 0025). A test checks that they are unbound.\n- The command called the obsolete alias `sia-vulpea-select-note`; it now calls `sp-collec-query-select-note`.\n- Literate doc (`sp-vulpea.org`) updated in bullets, and the `.el` re-tangled from it.\n- No key was bound to the old command, so there is no keybinding to change. The old `emacs-include` copy of the module is untouched.\n\n## Tested\n- `emacs --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-test.el`: 5 tests pass in Emacs 29.3 with Vulpea stubbed (meta-key detection, grouping and dedup, the Org buffer, old names gone).\n- **Not run** in the real Emacs on the Mac, or with the real vault. The `vulpea-db-query-links-to` link shape is still the unconfirmed assumption noted in the module.\n- Tangling only this doc; `tangle-all` rewrites many unrelated files (existing drift), which I left out.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAyV71uz259d2Xv3kV)_",
